  "notes": "Architecture major, no concentration (the standard pre-professional path). Built from the official 2026-2027 University Catalog PDF 'Architecture Major (No Concentration)' roadmap. Advancement to third-year professional level requires minimum 2.250 GPA in ARCH courses and minimum 2.500 overall GPA, with no more than one deficiency in required major coursework from the first four semesters. The roadmap prints ranges on some slots (MATH 12002 is 3-5 credits) and a minimum total of 124; the printed semester totals with minimum-credit options sum to 119, while the requirements table lists 14 non-architecture elective credits 'depending on earning 124 credit hours'. This plan models MATH 12002 Analytic Geometry and Calculus I at its standard 5 credits and distributes 15 non-architecture elective credits across the roadmap's elective slots (Sem 3: 1, Sem 4: 4, Sem 5: 1, Sem 6: 5, Sem 8: 4) to reach the catalog's 124 minimum -- the roadmap's elective slots are shown with these modeled values. Prerequisite chain follows the lockstep studio sequence (ARCH 10101 -> 10102 -> 20101 -> 20102 -> 30101 -> 30102 -> 40101 -> 40102), the structures sequence (ARCH 20301 -> 40301 -> 40302), materials/methods (ARCH 40401 -> 40402), environmental technology (ARCH 40501 -> 40502), physics (PHY 13001 + PHY 13021 -> PHY 13012), and MATH 12011 -> MATH 12002.",
